event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/plan.md\", \"content\": \"Plan for mission \\\"greet, tested\\\":\\n\\n1. Send dev a dispatch with the exact deliverable spec: src/greet.py containing\\n   greet(name) returning \\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\", and tests/test_greet.py covering a\\n   normal name and the empty string, such that `python3 -m unittest discover -s\\n   tests` exits 0. Ask dev to commit to its own branch and reply honestly.\\n2. Wait for dev's reply.\\n3. Judge by fetching dev's branch (not trusting the report): verify src/greet.py\\n   exists and implements greet as specified, verify tests/test_greet.py exists\\n   and covers both a normal name and the empty string, and actually run\\n   `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` against the fetched tree to confirm\\n   exit code 0.\\n4. Accept if and only if all three criteria hold. Otherwise send precise rework.\\n5. Once accepted, reply to mission m1 with --outcome campaign-met (or the\\n   appropriate alternative outcome if something remains unmet or the campaign\\n   stalls/is blocked before the deadline 2026-09-26T19:40:37Z).\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

